<https://w3id.org/era-aom/livestock/AOM_000368> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/era-aom/livestock/AOM_000366> ;
    skos:definition "Specific Growth Rate (SGR) is typically measured as the change in body weight of an animal over a specified time period, divided by the number of days in that period. For example, if an animal weighed 100 kg at the beginning of a 30-day period and weighed 120 kg at the end of that period, the SGR would be calculated as follows: SGR = (120 kg - 100 kg) ÷ 30 days = 0.67 kg/day.  This indicates that the animal gained an average of 0.67 kg per day during the 30-day period.  (human validated chatGPT)"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/era-aom/scheme/livestock-v2> ;
    skos:notation "AOM_000368" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Specific Growth Rate"@en ;
    era:conceptType "legacy_aom_concept" ;
    era:status "unknown" .

